Deriving an Untyped does not ask whether something made of it is left,
so the derived one, the whole of the memory, lies over what the source made before.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: memory that may hold kernel objects overlaps a node not above or below it

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -86,9 +86,6 @@ static int op_captable(struct thread *t, const struct cap *cap,
          * A derived Untyped is the whole of the memory, which only a free one has to give,
          * and the source makes nothing more while it lives, as for anything else it made.
          */
-        if (src.type == CAP_UNTYPED && !untyped_free(source)) {
-            return KERR_NO_MEMORY;
-        }
         return cap_store(table, arg[1], &src, source);
     }
     case OP_CAP_MOVE: {
